  "result": "Done! Added customer ID normalization to handle mixed case and whitespace.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **normalizeId() function** \u2014 In src/customers.js:\n   - Trims leading/trailing whitespace\n   - Converts to uppercase\n   - Handles 'c-007 ', ' c-007', 'c-007', or any combination\n\n2. **Updated getCustomer()** \u2014 Normalizes ID before lookup:\n   - Finds customers regardless of input case or spaces\n   - Example: getCustomer(' c-003 ') finds 'C-003'\n\n3. **Updated createInvoice()** \u2014 Normalizes customerId:\n   - Normalizes before validation and storage\n   - Stored invoice has the normalized customer ID\n   - Example: createInvoice({ customerId: 'c-001', ... }) stores 'C-001'\n\n4. **Test coverage** \u2014 9 new tests:\n   - normalizeId with spaces, lowercase, mixed case\n   - getCustomer with various ID formats\n   - createInvoice storing normalized IDs\n   - Uppercase/lowercase/spacing combinations\n\nAll 104 tests pass (9 new ID normalization tests + 95 previous).\n\n**Why this matters:**\n- Real systems often have inconsistent data entry ('c-007 ' vs 'C-007')\n- Normalization ensures consistent lookups and storage\n- No more failures due to whitespace or case mismatches\n- Single source of truth: all IDs stored and compared in uppercase, trimmed",
